  "proof": "The complete positive cell tables at the base point are as follows.\nThe omitted endpoint cells are zero:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|rrrrrrrr}\nG&\\varnothing&1&2&3&12&13&23&123\\\\ \\hline\np_G&M&0&0&0&0&0&0&0,\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|rrrrrrr}\nG&1&2&3&12&13&23&123\\\\ \\hline\nq_G&\n0&0&0&\n\\dfrac1{40950000}&\n\\dfrac{91}{3800900000}&\n\\dfrac{91}{750900000}&\n\\dfrac{262388347241}{1\\,298\\,613\\,593\\,550\\,000},\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|rrrrrrr}\nG&1&2&3&12&13&23&123\\\\ \\hline\nr_G&\n\\dfrac{3672919}{277200000}&\n\\dfrac{713864465256324149}{25226553717763200000}&\n\\dfrac{3\\,550\\,142\\,468\\,745\\,787}{60396653116800000}&\n\\dfrac{373231}{7200000}&\n\\dfrac{4078013}{190960000}&\n\\dfrac{66896669}{10606464000}&\n\\dfrac1{80000}.\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nThe merged-fan map for \\(B=(A_0+A_2)/2\\) is\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccccc}\nj&0&1&2&3&4&5&6&7&8\\\\ \\hline\n(\\iota_0(j),\\iota_2(j))&\n(0,0)&(1,1)&(2,1)&(3,1)&(3,2)&(4,2)&(5,2)&(6,2)&(6,0).\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\nThere is one shared fan ray,\n\\[\na_1-a_0=\\frac{3427063}{15592500}(1,-1),\n\\qquad q_1-q_0=\\frac1{2500}(1,-1).\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\nWriting\n\\(\\eta_{sj}=[k_{s+1}-k_s,b_j-k_s]\\), exact substitution gives\n\\[\n\\eta_{sj}=0\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n(s,j)\\in\\{(1,1),(1,2),(2,5),(2,6),(4,0),(4,8)\\}.\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\nEvery other \\(\\eta_{sj}\\) is strictly positive.  All nontrivial\nconvexity determinants of \\(A_0,A_2,K\\) are strictly positive, and\n\\[\n|K|-|B|\n=\\frac{10857958533043991051524802341}\n{186210071146483097313600000000}>0.\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\nConsequently (5) is the complete list of active inequality rows:\nthere is no active convexity row and no tight-middle row.\n\nHere are the exact cell-area derivative blocks.  Every coefficient not\nlisted is zero.  For \\(P=D|A_0|\\), in the local column order\n\\((\\alpha_{0x},\\alpha_{0y},\\ldots,\\alpha_{6x},\\alpha_{6y})\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|r@{\\quad}c|r}\n\\alpha_{0x}&-\\frac{327073}{770000}&\\alpha_{0y}&-\\frac{5463131}{114576000}\\\\\n\\alpha_{1x}&-\\frac{22346491}{386694000}&\\alpha_{1y}&-\\frac{18088489}{124740000}\\\\\n\\alpha_{2x}&\\frac{9453041204485193709791}{48492206027729973258750}&\n\\alpha_{2y}&-\\frac{54077}{770000}\\\\\n\\alpha_{3x}&\\frac{53981453}{214830000}&\\alpha_{3y}&-\\frac{54077}{1540000}\\\\\n\\alpha_{4x}&\\frac{231584404106031408659}{1007630255121661782000}&\n\\alpha_{4y}&\\frac{437}{9000}\\\\\n\\alpha_{5x}&\\frac{437}{3600}&\\alpha_{5y}&\\frac{877259}{7440000}\\\\\n\\alpha_{6x}&-\\frac{2805541}{8910000}&\\alpha_{6y}&\\frac{1172279}{8910000}\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{7}\n\\]\n\nFor the four positive \\(A_2\\)-cells, let \\(Q\\) have rows\n\\((Q_{12},Q_{13},Q_{23},Q_{123})\\) and local columns\n\\((\\theta_{0x},\\theta_{0y},\\theta_{1x},\\theta_{1y},\n\\theta_{2x},\\theta_{2y})\\).  Its sparse rows are\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|l}\n12&\n0:-\\frac{37991}{745290000},\\\n1:\\frac{2503}{248430000},\\\n2:\\frac{38009}{745290000},\\\n3:-\\frac{2497}{248430000},\\\n4:\\frac{181}{41405000},\\\n5:\\frac{181}{41405000}\\\\\n13&\n0:-\\frac1{20000},\\\n1:-\\frac1{20000},\\\n2:\\frac{37991}{760180000},\\\n3:-\\frac{5472819081}{28893681620000},\\\n4:\\frac9{380090000},\\\n5:-\\frac{67419}{14446840810000}\\\\\n23&\n0:-\\frac{436523027}{375900540000},\\\n1:\\frac{2497}{50060000},\\\n2:-\\frac1{20000},\\\n3:-\\frac1{20000},\\\n4:-\\frac{37991}{62650090000},\\\n5:\\frac3{25030000}\\\\\n123&\n0:-\\frac{655344559931027}{1\\,556\\,416\\,185\\,870\\,000},\\\n1:\\frac{17249994997}{207273430000},\\\n2:\\frac{1328479923991}{3147525290000},\\\n3:-\\frac{9\\,951\\,643\\,110\\,616\\,581}{119634288747610000},\\\n4:\\frac{1\\,934\\,571\\,908\\,592\\,839}{9859637134788805000},\\\n5:\\frac{29272712028475017}{149722312367633915000}.\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\n\nFor the seven middle cells, let \\(H\\) have rows\n\\((H_1,H_2,H_3,H_{12},H_{13},H_{23},H_{123})\\) and local columns\n\\((\\kappa_{0x},\\kappa_{0y},\\ldots,\\kappa_{4x},\\kappa_{4y})\\).\nIts sparse rows are\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|l}\n1&\n2:\\frac{60835}{3841992},\\\n3:-\\frac{81995}{7683984},\\\n4:\\frac{40223401}{364989240},\\\n5:-\\frac{225851833}{3649892400},\\\n6:\\frac{49}{376200},\\\n7:\\frac{49}{940500}\\\\\n2&\n0:-\\frac{5392206029396330621174885332327}{52874741907382958804565757916100},\\\n1:\\frac{264218095440420200437569381284023}{13112935993030973783532307963192800},\\\n4:\\frac1{376200},\\\n5:\\frac1{940500},\\\n6:\\frac{162965294209}{22604438815200},\\\n7:\\frac{2182564369393}{280295041308480},\\\n8:-\\frac{68676033105406797765034999751}{220351998687928140036391803360},\\\n9:\\frac{23838424421820366611536702406849}{341545597966288617056407295208000}\\\\\n3&\n0:-\\frac{289858294068843081992090963683}{918133327866367250151632514000},\\\n1:-\\frac{764353101504207894359456022761}{227697065310859078037604863472000},\\\n2:\\frac{18525382878573743}{381527167655153520},\\\n3:-\\frac{8\\,365\\,487\\,403\\,858\\,649}{70327588507862400},\\\n4:\\frac{129214}{9730125},\\\n5:-\\frac{2809}{313875},\\\n8:-\\frac{269917403946542654118722993189969}{4032338285989699996350327942830175},\\\n9:\\frac{1889421827625798578831060952329783}{142859984989349371299268761403126200}\\\\\n12&\n4:\\frac{25051}{100320},\\\n5:\\frac{25051}{250800},\\\n6:\\frac{43381}{167200},\\\n7:\\frac{43381}{418000}\\\\\n13&\n2:\\frac{15320185}{153839763},\\\n3:-\\frac{666095}{9925146},\\\n4:\\frac{73114102}{769198815},\\\n5:-\\frac{1589437}{24812865}\\\\\n23&\n0:-\\frac{6565282918608852056983}{117005791183449684958800},\\\n1:\\frac{321698863011833750792167}{29017436213495521869782400},\\\n8:-\\frac{108010178122146216220709}{2316714665432303762184240},\\\n9:\\frac{5292498727985164594814741}{574545237027211333021691520}\\\\\n123&0.\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{9}\n\\]\nThe last row is zero because the \\(123\\)-cell is the fixed triangle\ncut out by the three lines \\(y_i=t\\), strictly inside \\(K\\).\n\nEmbed \\(P,Q_G,H_G\\) in \\(\\mathbb Q^{30}\\) in their corresponding\ncoordinate blocks.  The three exact crossing rows are\n\\[\nC_i=-\\frac29P+\n\\sum_{G\\in\\{12,13,23,123\\}}\n\\left({\\bf1}_{i\\in G}-\\frac29\\right)Q_G+\n\\sum_{G\\in\\{1,2,3,12,13,23,123\\}}\n\\left({\\bf1}_{i\\in G}-\\frac29\\right)H_G\n\\quad(i=1,2,3).\n\\tag{10}\n\\]\nThis is the derivative of the crossing identity from\n`89563f2f27529ab0`; the \\(A_0\\) cap derivatives vanish on this\nstratum.\n\nThe six endpoint cut-incidence rows, scaled without changing their\nzero sets, are\n\\[\nZ_0=\\alpha_{0x}+\\alpha_{0y},\\quad\nZ_1=\\alpha_{1x}+\\alpha_{1y},\\quad\nZ_2=\\alpha_{3x},\\quad Z_3=\\alpha_{4x},\\quad\nZ_4=\\alpha_{5y},\\quad Z_5=\\alpha_{6y}.\n\\tag{11}\n\\]\nThey retain the three boundary pieces \\(y_3=p,y_1=p,y_2=p\\).\nThe shared-fan row obtained by differentiating (4) is\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nF={}&\\frac1{2500}\n(\\alpha_{0x}+\\alpha_{0y}-\\alpha_{1x}-\\alpha_{1y})\\\\\n&-\\frac{3427063}{15592500}(\\theta_{0x}+\\theta_{0y})\n+\\frac{3427063}{15592500}(\\theta_{1x}+\\theta_{1y}).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{12}\n\\]\nThus the complete equality matrix, in literal row order, is\n\\[\nE=\\operatorname{rows}\n\\bigl(P,Q_{12},Q_{13},Q_{23},Q_{123},\nH_1,H_2,H_3,H_{12},H_{13},H_{23},H_{123},\nC_1,C_2,C_3,Z_0,\\ldots,Z_5,F\\bigr).\n\\tag{13}\n\\]\nThis is a \\(22\\times30\\) rational matrix of exact rank \\(18\\).\nThe zero first derivatives of the absent cells add only zero rows.\n\nFor the inequality matrix, use the active-contact row order in (5),\nfollowed by the capacity row.  The six nonzero rows are below; again,\nunlisted coefficients are zero:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|l}\n(1,1)&\n\\alpha_{1x}:-\\frac{207}{1000},\\\n\\alpha_{1y}:\\frac{279}{2000},\\\n\\theta_{1x}:-\\frac{207}{1000},\\\n\\theta_{1y}:\\frac{279}{2000},\\\n\\kappa_{1x}:\\frac{1909}{4620},\\\n\\kappa_{1y}:-\\frac{2573}{9240},\\\n\\kappa_{2x}:\\frac{23}{28875},\\\n\\kappa_{2y}:-\\frac{31}{57750}\\\\\n(1,2)&\n\\alpha_{2x}:-\\frac{207}{1000},\\\n\\alpha_{2y}:\\frac{279}{2000},\\\n\\theta_{1x}:-\\frac{207}{1000},\\\n\\theta_{1y}:\\frac{279}{2000},\\\n\\kappa_{1x}:\\frac{25858187}{71610000},\\\n\\kappa_{1y}:-\\frac{1124269}{4620000},\\\n\\kappa_{2x}:\\frac{3788353}{71610000},\\\n\\kappa_{2y}:-\\frac{164711}{4620000}\\\\\n(2,5)&\n\\alpha_{4x}:-\\frac{209}{800},\\\n\\alpha_{4y}:-\\frac{209}{2000},\\\n\\theta_{2x}:-\\frac{209}{800},\\\n\\theta_{2y}:-\\frac{209}{2000},\\\n\\kappa_{2x}:\\frac{21}{100},\\\n\\kappa_{2y}:\\frac{21}{250},\\\n\\kappa_{3x}:\\frac5{16},\\\n\\kappa_{3y}:\\frac18\\\\\n(2,6)&\n\\alpha_{5x}:-\\frac{209}{800},\\\n\\alpha_{5y}:-\\frac{209}{2000},\\\n\\theta_{2x}:-\\frac{209}{800},\\\n\\theta_{2y}:-\\frac{209}{2000},\\\n\\kappa_{2x}:\\frac{319}{3600},\\\n\\kappa_{2y}:\\frac{319}{9000},\\\n\\kappa_{3x}:\\frac{781}{1800},\\\n\\kappa_{3y}:\\frac{781}{4500}\\\\\n(4,0)&\n\\alpha_{0x}:\\frac{32501608662069356933}{75449875730513684400},\\\n\\alpha_{0y}:-\\frac{227511260634485498531}{2673081311595341961600},\\\n\\theta_{0x}:\\frac{32501608662069356933}{75449875730513684400},\\\n\\theta_{0y}:-\\frac{227511260634485498531}{2673081311595341961600},\\\n\\kappa_{0x}:-\\frac{134756035135163}{161056626558300},\\\n\\kappa_{0y}:\\frac{6\\,603\\,045\\,721\\,622\\,987}{39942043386458400},\\\n\\kappa_{4x}:-\\frac{24656358447199}{992526450715800},\\\n\\kappa_{4y}:\\frac{172594509130393}{35163794253931200}\\\\\n(4,8)&\n\\alpha_{6x}:\\frac{32501608662069356933}{75449875730513684400},\\\n\\alpha_{6y}:-\\frac{227511260634485498531}{2673081311595341961600},\\\n\\theta_{0x}:\\frac{32501608662069356933}{75449875730513684400},\\\n\\theta_{0y}:-\\frac{227511260634485498531}{2673081311595341961600},\\\n\\kappa_{0x}:-\\frac{2\\,801\\,441\\,466\\,230\\,089}{5\\,368\\,554\\,218\\,610\\,000},\\\n\\kappa_{0y}:\\frac{137270631845274361}{1331401446215280000},\\\n\\kappa_{4x}:-\\frac{16858932687049379}{49626322535790000},\\\n\\kappa_{4y}:\\frac{118012528809345653}{1758189712696560000}.\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{14}\n\\]\n\nFor completeness, put \\(S=f_2,T=f_3\\).  The strict sign pairs\n\\((\\operatorname{sgn}S(b_j),\\operatorname{sgn}T(b_j))\\), for\n\\(j=0,\\ldots,8\\), are\n\\[\n(+,-),(+,-),(+,-),(+,-),(-,+),(-,+),(-,+),(-,+),(-,-).\n\\tag{15}\n\\]\nHence every one of the nine \\(B\\)-edges is charging.  Therefore\n\\[\nZ=\\{S,T\\geq0\\}\\cap\\bigcap_{j=0}^8\\{\\lambda_j\\leq0\\}\n=B\\cap\\{S,T\\geq0\\}=W\n\\]\nthroughout a sufficiently small fixed-sign neighborhood, and\n\\[\n|Z|=|W|=\n\\frac{266217609946578874416636113467912863025299525049}\n{390200413107232474023071301812968133700684000000000}.\n\\tag{16}\n\\]\nThe capacity derivative is consequently the zero row.  Thus\n\\[\nG=\\operatorname{rows}\n\\bigl(g_{(1,1)},g_{(1,2)},g_{(2,5)},g_{(2,6)},\ng_{(4,0)},g_{(4,8)},0\\bigr).\n\\tag{17}\n\\]\n\nThe release row for \\(a_2=u\\), whose neighbors are \\(a_1,a_3\\), has\nthe following six nonzero coefficients:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|rrrrrr}\n&\\alpha_{1x}&\\alpha_{1y}&\\alpha_{2x}&\\alpha_{2y}\n&\\alpha_{3x}&\\alpha_{3y}\\\\ \\hline\n\\mathcal R&\n\\dfrac{55410437860995672319297}{193968824110919893035000}&\n-\\dfrac{54077}{770000}&\n-\\dfrac{9453041204485193709791}{24246103013864986629375}&\n\\dfrac{54077}{385000}&\n\\dfrac{1243771}{11935000}&\n-\\dfrac{54077}{770000}.\n\\end{array}\n\\tag{18}\n\\]\nThis is exactly\n\\(-D[a_2-a_1,a_3-a_2]\\).\n\nIt remains only to verify (1).  In (7), its two nonzero contributions\nare\n\\[\n-\\frac{54077}{770000}\\frac{192500}{54077}\n-\\frac{54077}{1540000}\\left(-\\frac{385000}{54077}\\right)\n=-\\frac14+\\frac14=0.\n\\tag{19}\n\\]\nThus \\(P\\xi=0\\).  The endpoint-cut row \\(\\alpha_{3x}=0\\) is preserved,\nand every other row in (11) and (12) is unaffected.  Since \\(A_2\\)\nand \\(K\\) are fixed, (8) and (9) vanish on \\(\\xi\\).  Equation (10)\nthen gives \\(C_i\\xi=0\\) for all three crossings.  Hence \\(E\\xi=0\\).\n\nAmong the rows of (14), only the contact \\((1,2)\\) changes:\n\\[\ng_{(1,2)}\\xi\n=\\frac{279}{2000}\\frac{192500}{54077}\n=\\frac{107415}{216308}>0,\n\\tag{20}\n\\]\nwhile the other five contact rows and the capacity row are zero.\nTherefore \\(G\\xi\\geq0\\).  Finally, (18) gives\n\\[\n\\mathcal R\\xi\n=\\frac{54077}{385000}\\frac{192500}{54077}\n-\\frac{54077}{770000}\\left(-\\frac{385000}{54077}\\right)\n=\\frac12+\\frac12=1.\n\\tag{21}\n\\]\nThis directly proves exact rational feasibility, without using a\nfloating-point LP status.\n\nThe fixed-stratum formulas used to obtain the rows are correct at this\nrealization.  Their phrase \u201call other exact incidence rows\u201d is\nessential here: it contributes the six rows (11) and the shared-fan\nrow (12).  Omitting (12) would fail to instantiate the declared\nnine-vertex merged-fan stratum.  Exact half-plane clipping and the\nshoelace derivative over \\(\\mathbb Q\\) reproduce (2), (7)--(9),\n(14), and (16).  SageMath 10.8 was used only as an exact rational\naudit of those displayed data; equations (19)--(21) are the direct\ncertificate.\n",
