  "statement": "Use the realization of accepted fact `0c0621b05f1db4ff`, with the\ncrossing convention of accepted fact `89563f2f27529ab0`.  In\n\\((y_1,y_2)\\)-coordinates put \\(y_3=1-y_1-y_2\\) and\n\\[\n f_i=-200y_i+\\frac{199}{3},\\qquad\n p=\\frac{199}{300},\\qquad t=\\frac{199}{600}.\n\\]\nIndex the endpoint vertices counterclockwise as\n\\[\n A_0=(a_0,\\ldots,a_6)=(F_0,F_1,u,v,F_3,F_4,F_5),\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nF_0&=\\left(\\frac{1350241}{4455000},\\frac{149609}{4455000}\\right),&\nF_1&=\\left(\\frac{603919}{1155000},-\\frac{215069}{1155000}\\right),\\\\\nF_2&=\\left(\\frac{199}{300},\\frac{10331}{465000}\\right),&\nF_3&=\\left(\\frac{199}{300},\\frac{757}{1800}\\right),\\\\\nF_4&=\\left(\\frac{637}{1125},\\frac{199}{300}\\right),&\nF_5&=\\left(\\frac{1590341}{3720000},\\frac{199}{300}\\right),\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\theta=\\frac{228549000559154512729}{501722218124117618589},\n\\qquad\nu=\\frac{F_1+F_2}{2},\\qquad\nv=(1-\\theta)F_2+\\theta F_3.\n\\]\nIndex\n\\[\nA_2=(q_0,q_1,q_2)=\n\\left(\n\\left(-\\frac1{5000},\\frac1{5000}\\right),\n\\left(\\frac1{5000},-\\frac1{5000}\\right),\n\\left(\\frac16,\\frac{38}{45}\\right)\n\\right).\n\\]\nFinally put\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nw_1&=\\left(\\frac{27}{50},\\frac8{25}\\right),&\nw_2&=\\left(\\frac8{25},\\frac{87}{100}\\right),&\nw_3&=\\left(\\frac3{40},-\\frac{37}{100}\\right),\\\\\n\\lambda_2&=\\frac{880933660331}{66570072310764},&\n\\lambda_3&=\\frac{359343325156337}{8\\cdot153841599860949},\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\ne_{20}&=\\frac{19}{20}w_2+\\frac1{20}w_1,&\ne_{23}&=(1-\\lambda_2)w_2+\\lambda_2w_3,\\\\\ne_{30}&=\\frac35w_3+\\frac25w_1,&\ne_{32}&=(1-\\lambda_3)w_3+\\lambda_3w_2,\n\\end{aligned}\n\\qquad\nK=(k_0,\\ldots,k_4)=(e_{32},e_{30},w_1,e_{20},e_{23}).\n\\]\n\nOrder the thirty velocity coordinates as\n\\[\n\\xi=(\\alpha_{0x},\\alpha_{0y},\\ldots,\\alpha_{6x},\\alpha_{6y},\n\\theta_{0x},\\theta_{0y},\\ldots,\\theta_{2x},\\theta_{2y},\n\\kappa_{0x},\\kappa_{0y},\\ldots,\\kappa_{4x},\\kappa_{4y}).\n\\]\nLet \\(E,G,\\mathcal R\\) be the exact matrices specified in the proof\nbelow.  Then\n\\[\n E\\xi=0,\\qquad G\\xi\\geq0,\\qquad \\mathcal R\\xi\\geq1\n\\]\nis feasible.  One solution is\n\\[\n\\alpha_2=\\left(0,\\frac{192500}{54077}\\right),\\qquad\n\\alpha_3=\\left(0,-\\frac{385000}{54077}\\right),\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nwith every other \\(\\alpha_i,\\theta_i,\\kappa_i\\) equal to zero.  Here\n\\(a_2=u\\) is the declared deletable unmarked vertex.\n",
